WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:07.920
And now, my friends, there are different types of databases, so let's see what we have.

00:07.960 --> 00:12.000
The first and the most famous one, it is the relational database.

00:12.000 --> 00:12.800
It is very simple.

00:12.800 --> 00:16.840
It is like spreadsheets call them table where we have columns and rows.

00:16.880 --> 00:21.520
And then there is like a relationship between those tables to describe how they relate to each other.

00:21.560 --> 00:23.880
And that's why we call it relational database.

00:23.880 --> 00:27.040
So if people hear a database they're going to think about this one.

00:27.040 --> 00:30.000
Now we have another type of databases called key value.

00:30.040 --> 00:35.320
This time the data is organized completely different where you have pairs of keys and values.

00:35.360 --> 00:35.960
Think about it.

00:35.960 --> 00:40.920
It's like a big dictionary where you have a word like the key and the definition of the word.

00:40.920 --> 00:41.800
This is the value.

00:41.840 --> 00:43.080
And now moving on to the next one.

00:43.080 --> 00:45.320
This is as well important column based.

00:45.360 --> 00:51.360
So now instead of grouping the data by the rows, this type of databases group the data into columns.

00:51.360 --> 00:53.000
That's why it's called column based.

00:53.000 --> 00:58.160
And this is very advanced database in order to handle huge amounts of data where the main purpose is

00:58.160 --> 00:59.360
to search for data.

00:59.400 --> 01:02.160
Moving on to another database called Graph database.

01:02.160 --> 01:05.320
The main focus here is the relationship between objects.

01:05.320 --> 01:08.390
So the main idea here is how to connect my data points.

01:08.430 --> 01:11.470
And now finally we have the document database.

01:11.470 --> 01:16.430
The data is stored as entire documents where the structure of the data is not that important.

01:16.430 --> 01:19.950
What is more important is to fit everything in one page, in one document.

01:19.950 --> 01:25.230
And now if you look to those five types, we can group the document graph, column based key value.

01:25.270 --> 01:31.910
All those databases called NoSQL databases and the relational database is SQL database.

01:31.910 --> 01:35.430
And in this course we will be focusing of course on the relational database.

01:35.430 --> 01:41.710
And I'm sure you have heard about like the Microsoft SQL server, the MySQL, the PostgreSQL, all those

01:41.710 --> 01:44.910
databases, they are SQL relational database.

01:44.910 --> 01:48.710
And for the key value you have the Redis, the Amazon DynamoDB.

01:48.750 --> 01:52.070
And we have for the column based, we have the Cassandra and the redshift.

01:52.070 --> 01:58.390
For the graph database, we have the Neo4j's and the very famous database, the MongoDB as a document

01:58.390 --> 01:59.150
database.

01:59.190 --> 02:04.550
Now my friends, for this course we're going to be focusing on the SQL relational databases because

02:04.550 --> 02:08.230
it is the most famous one and the most used one in companies.

02:08.230 --> 02:11.070
And I will be focusing on the Microsoft SQL server.

02:11.070 --> 02:13.550
So those are the different types of databases.
